daemon: Park a still drag instead of releasing it, add a drag debug log

Chris: lifting the finger to continue a selection (click and drag past the pad
edge) ended the drag; libinput saw the release before the finger came back.

Causes found in the pkgrel 13 latch:

 - The stillness rule (bit released, contacts still for DragReleaseStillMs)
   released the button. A pause at the pad edge before lifting is exactly that
   state, so the drag was over before DragRelatchMs could start. A drag whose
   stillness rule fires is now parked instead: the button stays held, and it
   ends only if the finger stays parked and still for another DragRelatchMs, or
   if the finger lifts and does not come back within DragRelatchMs. Lifting
   starts the relatch wait as usual, moving again or a new firmware press
   un-parks the drag. DragRelatchMs = 0 keeps the old behaviour (release).
   DragReleaseStillMs = 0 still means: never release because of stillness
   (it was never treated as "release at once").
 - While the drag waited for the finger to come back, frames with an invalid
   contact (a landing finger at the pad edge fails the size / aspect check) ended
   the drag after DRAG_BLOCK_GRACE_MS. They now leave the wait window to decide,
   which keeps running during such frames.
 - A firmware press during the wait or parked state is absorbed as before; it
   is not processed as a new press.

New [Touchpad] DragDebug (default false), or the environment variable
IPTSD_SL7_DRAG_DEBUG=1: every latch transition is logged with a timestamp, the
reason and the state (firmware bit, button, latch, wait, park, contacts,
ghosts): firmware bit edges and how they were handled, BTN_LEFT down / up with
the reason, latch, park, unpark, wait start, resume, palm block start / end,
contact count changes while a drag is latched, and why a drag ended.

